## Why This Is Asked

Backpressure in streaming pipelines is a common real-world pain point; this question probes ability to model skew, test end-to-end latency, and reason about autoscaling and resilience under bursts.

## Key Concepts

- Backpressure, end-to-end latency, tail latency
- Autoscaling of Kafka, Spark, and storage
- Throughput under burst, circuit breakers, graceful degradation

## Code Example

```javascript
function percentile(arr, p) {
  if (!Array.isArray(arr) || arr.length === 0) return 0;
  const sorted = arr.slice().sort((a,b)=>a-b);
  const idx = Math.ceil(p/100 * sorted.length) - 1;
  return sorted[Math.max(0, Math.min(idx, sorted.length-1))];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you instrument latency tracking across components?
- How would you simulate bursty workloads without real traffic?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess end-to-end latency across a fan-out path, backpressure resilience, region-aware autoscaling, and observability for a large-scale chat system with moderation integration.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end latency and tail behavior (P99/P99.9)
- Backpressure and queue depth management
- Region-aware autoscaling and load distribution
- Observability: tracing, metrics, dashboards, and alerting
- Fault injection: moderation outages, latency spikes, network partitions

## Code Example

```javascript
// P99 latency measurement sketch
function onMessageSent(event) {
  const t0 = performance.now();
  deliverToRecipients(event);
  const latency = performance.now() - t0;
  recordMetric('e2e_latency_ms', latency);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you model and test regional failover guarantees?
- What telemetry would you add to differentiate moderation latency from delivery latency?
